<title>FRANCE: Sanofi sees 97 results rise in line 1996.</title>
<headline>Sanofi sees 97 results rise in line 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pharmaceuticals firm Sanofi expects a rise in 1997 pre-exceptional results in line with that seen last year, chairman Jean-Francois Dehecq said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;A favourable start to 1997 allows us to believe that, if nothing changes,&quot; the increase in 1997 results &quot;will be of the same order of magnitude&quot; as for 1996, he told the annual shareholders meeting.</p>
<p>Sanofi, in which Elf Aquitaine holds a 55 percent stake, reported an 11 percent increase in 1996 net profit to 1.74 billion francs and saw turnover rising 3.2 percent to 23.64 billion francs.</p>
</text>
